{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Active: 9+16+30+37+51+58 = 201.\n\n9+16=25, +30=55, +37=92, +51=143, +58=201.","thinkingSignature":"5a99c362-1b27-443c-9086-bdfed725cacc"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_s084fit11QJRwrOow3zv2423","name":"experience","arguments":{"op":"put","id":"ledger-api-sum-active","title":"Local mock \"ledger\" API: discovery + paginated sum procedure","content":"ENVIRONMENT: local mock API \"ledger\" v1 (api.json: {service:ledger, version:1}; GET /info -> {version:1,documentation:\"api.json\"}). Endpoints: GET /items (page 1-based, limit max 3) -> {items:[{id,amount,active}], total, next_page}. next_page null ends list; page past end -> {items:[],next_page:null}. Extra params ignored; no multi-ledger selector.\nPROCEDURE (sum active amounts): iterate page=1,2,... accumulating items where active==true; stop when next_page null or items empty. Same pattern for count/filter.\nEVIDENCE: datasets have 8 items over 3 pages (limit 3) with ids prefixed per-ledger e.g. \"item-1-\", \"item-2-\". Observed run item-1-* active sum=195 (8,15,29,36,50,57); run item-2-* active sum=201 (9,16,30,37,51,58); inactive every 3rd (items 3 and 6). Each dataset: 6 active, 2 inactive; active amounts increase by 7.\nCAVEATS: 'total'=8 is total item count, NOT active count/sum. Do not assume dataset identity; always re-fetch all pages. limit>3, alternate ledgers, other versions untested."}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"experiment","model":"deepseek-flash","usage":{"input":177,"output":452,"cacheRead":1664,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":2293,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790914837341,"responseId":"5a99c362-1b27-443c-9086-bdfed725cacc","rawStopReason":"tool_use","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_00_s084fit11QJRwrOow3zv2423","toolName":"experience","args":{"op":"put","id":"ledger-api-sum-active","title":"Local mock \"ledger\" API: discovery + paginated sum procedure","content":"ENVIRONMENT: local mock API \"ledger\" v1 (api.json: {service:ledger, version:1}; GET /info -> {version:1,documentation:\"api.json\"}). Endpoints: GET /items (page 1-based, limit max 3) -> {items:[{id,amount,active}], total, next_page}. next_page null ends list; page past end -> {items:[],next_page:null}. Extra params ignored; no multi-ledger selector.\nPROCEDURE (sum active amounts): iterate page=1,2,... accumulating items where active==true; stop when next_page null or items empty. Same pattern for count/filter.\nEVIDENCE: datasets have 8 items over 3 pages (limit 3) with ids prefixed per-ledger e.g. \"item-1-\", \"item-2-\". Observed run item-1-* active sum=195 (8,15,29,36,50,57); run item-2-* active sum=201 (9,16,30,37,51,58); inactive every 3rd (items 3 and 6). Each dataset: 6 active, 2 inactive; active amounts increase by 7.\nCAVEATS: 'total'=8 is total item count, NOT active count/sum. Do not assume dataset identity; always re-fetch all pages. limit>3, alternate ledgers, other versions untested."}}
